<title>USA: MGE wheat/barley/shrimp deliveries - Sept 27.</title>
<headline>MGE wheat/barley/shrimp deliveries - Sept 27.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Minneapolis Grain Exchange Grain reported the following deliveries against September futures (wheat in 000 bu, shrimp in lots) -</p>
<p>SPRING WHEAT - 355. All contracts filled.</p>
<p>Delivered Minneapolis/St Paul 220,000 bu.</p>
<p>Delivered Duluth/Superior 135,000 bu.</p>
<p>Delivered - AGP Grain/h 135, Continental Grain/h 220.</p>
<p>Received - Atwood Commodities/h 330, Cargill Investor Services/h 25..</p>
<p>WHITE WHEAT - 375. All contracts filled.</p>
<p>Delivered - Benson-Quinn/h 290, Benson-Quinn/c 85.</p>
<p>Received - Country Hedging/c 180, LFG/c 195.</p>
<p>BLACK TIGER SHRIMP - 2 lots. All contracts filled.</p>
<p>Delivered - Cargill Investor Services/c 2.</p>
<p>Received - Cargill Investor Services/c 2.</p>
<p>BARLEY - Nil. Oldest long - Aug 2, 1996.</p>
<p>WHITE SHRIMP - Nil.</p>
<p>H=House. C=Customer account.</p>
<p>(Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720)</p>
</text>
